    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG McCormack Properties are delighted to present this truly exceptional detached family home to the market. Set on approximately 0.52 acres of beautifully landscaped grounds, \"Tintean\"—the Irish word for hearth—perfectly embodies the warmth, comfort, and character that define this remarkable residence.\n\nOriginally built in 1976, this impressive, detached bungalow is set well back from the road on a mature, private site enclosed by established trees and hedging, creating a peaceful and secluded oasis, just 1.8km from the vibrant village of Clane.\n\nInternally, the property offers spacious, light-filled accommodation comprising four generous bedrooms, three stylishly redesigned bathrooms, a fitted kitchen with an electric aga, fully equipped utility room, a dedicated home office, and an attached garage with external access. The garage, office, and adjoining spaces offer excellent potential for reconfiguration or integration into the main living accommodation, allowing the home to adapt to a growing family's needs.\n\nThe exterior is even more impressive. Accessed via electric gates, the property is approached by a sweeping tarmac driveway bordered by mature hedging and attractive shrubbery. The expansive grounds feature beautifully maintained lawns, ample parking, and generous patio areas perfectly positioned to enjoy the sun well into the evening along with a greenhouse for the keen gardener.\n\nOffering an exceptional combination of privacy, quality, space, and convenience, this is a rare opportunity to acquire a distinguished family home in one of the area's most sought-after locations.\n\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate everything this outstanding property has to offer. To arrange a viewing, contact DNG McCormack Properties on 045 832535."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall - 2.66m x 4.68m\nL shaped, carpeted, coving and recess lighting, open welcoming area, storage press\n\nSitting Room/ Dining Room - 4.65m x 8.77m\nLarge open area, dual aspect windows, patio doors to side, split level, coving, and recess lighting, feature mounted solid fuel insert stove in red brick surround and slate hearth, carpeted flooring\n\nKitchen - 4.69m x 3.62m\nRedone in 2006, solid oak flooring, fully fitted kitchen units at floor & eye level, extensive storage, granite worktops, 2 sinks, sink aerator, mixer tap, recess lighting, door to rear patio\n\nUtility Room - 1.39m x 1.95m\nSolid oak flooring, granite worktop, storage area, plumbed for services, window\n\nBathroom - 1.77m x 3.56m\nOrnate floor tiles, tiled shower area, sunken jacuzzi bath with overhead electric shower, wooden panelling, window & velux window\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.46m x 4.17m\nLuxurious carpet, double doors to rear patio, coving, recess lighting\n\nEnsuite Wetroom - 3.54m x 1.77m\nModern & chic, fully tiled ceramic floor and wall tiles, WC (dual Flush), WHB, large walk in power shower, velux window, pocket door, old style balmoral cast iron radiator\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.59m x 3.56m\nLuxurious carpet, large sliderobes storage unit, coving, recess lighting\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.87m x 3.66m\nLuxurious carpet, floor to ceiling sliderobes, coving, recess lighting\n\nGuest WC/ Bathroom - 2.23m x 0.98m\nTiled flooring and shower area, extractor fan, WC, WHB, recess lighting\n\nBedroom 4 - 4.27m x 2.62m\nLuxurious carpet, floor to ceiling sliderobes, coving, recess lighting\n\nOffice - 3.55m x 3.33m\nCarpeted flooring, accessed externally, suitable for a multitude of uses, could be incorporated into house configuration, recess lighting\n\nGarage - 3.68m x 3.02m\nSockets, lighting, could be incorporated as part of the house for extra living space\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> 4 bedroom detached bungalow</li><li> Set on c. 0.52 acre site</li><li> Commanding views of the countryside</li><li> Only 1.3km to Clane village</li><li> Extends to an impressive 162m2/ 180m2 including office and garage</li><li> OFCH- Boiler only 1 yerar old</li><li> Excellent condition with remodeeled kitchen and bathrooms</li><li> Luxurious carpet flooring in bedrooms</li><li> C3 BER rating</li><li> Large front and rear lawns</li><li> Electric gates</li><li> External lighting, sockets and water</li><li> Greenhouse & Gazebo</li><li> Tarmac driveway</li><li> Mature hedging, shrubbery and bedding</li><li> Three patio areas utilising the flow of sunshine</ul>"
      },
